<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The integration of blockchain into the renewable energy sector holds immense potential, especially in managing the diverse nature of renewable energy sources like solar, wind, hydro, and biomass. These sources, often distributed across wide geographic areas, involve numerous stakeholders including energy producers, consumers, grid operators, and regulatory bodies. Blockchain technology can streamline interactions among these stakeholders, enhance energy distribution efficiency, and support the development of decentralised energy systems.)
/E (The integration of blockchain into the renewable energy sector holds immense potential, especially in managing the diverse nature of renewable energy sources like solar, wind, hydro, and biomass. These sources, often distributed across wide geographic areas, involve numerous stakeholders including energy producers, consumers, grid operators, and regulatory bodies. Blockchain technology can streamline interactions among these stakeholders, enhance energy distribution efficiency, and support the development of decentralised energy systems.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
