<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The most common consensus mechanisms are Proof-of-Work \(PoW\) and Proof-of-Stake \(PoS\), each with distinct implications for energy consumption and environmental impact. Various alternative consensus mechanisms also exist, e.g., Proof-of-Authority \(PoA\), Proof-of-Burn \(PoB\), and Proof-of-Capacity \(PoC\), among others; however, these are not as commonly used due to reasons such as limited utility, niche use-cases, or vulnerabilities such as economic inefficiencies, implementation complexity or governance issues. For the purposes of this paper, we provide an overview of the PoW and PoS consensus mechanisms, considering their large-scale use:)
/E (The most common consensus mechanisms are Proof-of-Work \(PoW\) and Proof-of-Stake \(PoS\), each with distinct implications for energy consumption and environmental impact. Various alternative consensus mechanisms also exist, e.g., Proof-of-Authority \(PoA\), Proof-of-Burn \(PoB\), and Proof-of-Capacity \(PoC\), among others; however, these are not as commonly used due to reasons such as limited utility, niche use-cases, or vulnerabilities such as economic inefficiencies, implementation complexity or governance issues. For the purposes of this paper, we provide an overview of the PoW and PoS consensus mechanisms, considering their large-scale use:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
